<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-ingredients-you-ll-need">Ingredients You&rsquo;ll Need</h2>



<p>Some recipes you&rsquo;ll find online refer to this recipe as &ldquo;3-ingredient egg bites&rdquo; because it uses three simple ingredients: eggs, cottage cheese, and shredded cheddar cheese.&nbsp;</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Cottage-Cheese-Egg-Bites-ingredients-1200x800.jpg" alt="Ingredients for eggs with cottage cheese bites with text on the image." class="wp-image-83959" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Cottage-Cheese-Egg-Bites-ingredients.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Cottage-Cheese-Egg-Bites-ingredients-400x267.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Cottage-Cheese-Egg-Bites-ingredients-768x512.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Cottage-Cheese-Egg-Bites-ingredients-150x100.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Cottage-Cheese-Egg-Bites-ingredients.jpg"></figure>



<p>From there, you can mix in your favorite vegetables or breakfast meats to make it your own. You&rsquo;ll find the exact measurements in the recipe card below, but here are a few helpful notes from my recipe testing:</p>



<p><strong>Eggs:</strong> I recommend using large organic eggs. </p>


<div class="block-tip cwp-inner is-style-border has-background has-senary-background-color">

<p><strong>How about using egg whites?</strong> While it won&rsquo;t be as fluffy, you can increase the protein by using a mix of whole eggs and egg whites (4 whole eggs and 4 egg whites). I wouldn&rsquo;t recommend using only egg whites because without the yolks, it loses that soft, custardy texture and rich taste that make it so satisfying.</p>

</div>


<p><strong>Cottage Cheese: </strong>During recipe testing, I found that full-fat (4%) cottage cheese yields the creamiest, custardiest results. That said, I have also made these mini egg bites with 2% cottage cheese. They were less creamy, but they still tasted good. </p>



<p>You can use both small and large curd cottage cheese.</p>



<p>Be sure to strain it if it has any excess liquid, so the egg mixture is not too watery. Additionally, some cottage cheeses can be saltier than others, so give yours a quick taste before adding extra salt to the mixture.&nbsp;</p>



<p><strong>Cheese:</strong> I am using freshly shredded cheddar cheese, but if you&rsquo;re wondering about the best cheese for egg bites, mozzarella, Monterey Jack, Parmesan, or gruyere cheese all work well. Feel free to mix a couple of cheeses together for extra depth.&nbsp;</p>



<p>If you have the time, shred your own cheese as store-bought pre-shredded cheeses contain anti-caking agents that prevent even melting and the creaminess of these egg and cottage cheese bites.</p>



<p><strong>Spinach:</strong> I opted for baby spinach as it is quick and easy to incorporate into the cottage cheese egg bites. I buy prewashed spinach that is sold in stores to save time.&nbsp;</p>



<p>If you prefer to wash your own, be sure to rinse and drain well before adding it into the egg mixture to prevent egg bites from turning watery.</p>



<p><strong>Seasonings:</strong> I kept it simple with kosher salt, black pepper, garlic powder, and paprika. But feel free to adjust to match the flavors you enjoy. You can add onion powder, red pepper flakes, or even a small amount of dried herbs like parsley, dill, oregano, or thyme.</p>


<div class="su-note" style="border-color:#d9d8d7;border-radius:1px;-moz-border-radius:1px;-webkit-border-radius:1px;"><div class="su-note-inner su-u-clearfix su-u-trim" style="background-color:#f3f2f1;border-color:#ffffff;color:#000;border-radius:1px;-moz-border-radius:1px;-webkit-border-radius:1px;">



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-add-ins-and-flavor-ideas">Add-Ins and Flavor Ideas</h3>



<p>These egg bites with cottage cheese are so easy to make, and there&rsquo;s plenty of room to get creative. Here are a few of my favorite ways to change them up:</p>



<p><strong>Breakfast meats:</strong> You can add about 1 cup of crumbled baked turkey bacon, regular bacon, cooked sausage (both pork and chicken would work), or diced ham.&nbsp;</p>



<p><strong>Potatoes and chives:</strong> If you love Starbucks&rsquo; Potato and Chive Egg Bites, you can easily recreate their flavor at home with this recipe. Cut a small yellow potato into &frac12;-inch cubes and saut&eacute; them in a bit of oil until tender. Once cooled, stir them into the egg mixture along with a handful of chopped chives.</p>



<p><strong>Other vegetables:</strong> Lighter vegetables, such as mushrooms, cherry tomatoes, or baby spinach, work best. Heavier vegetables, such as broccoli or bell peppers, can be used, but I recommend chopping them finely before adding them to the egg mixture. Stick to about 1 cup of vegetables so the bites don&rsquo;t get weighed down.</p>



<p>Frozen vegetables would also work (such as frozen spinach); however, be sure to thaw them and squeeze out all the liquid before adding them to the egg mixture.</p>


</div></div>
</div>



