<div id="recipe-83972-notes" class="wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Notes</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-notes"><ul>
<li><strong>Yields:</strong> This recipe makes 12 egg and cottage cheese bites ideal for 4 servings. The nutritional values below are for 3 egg bites (per serving).</li>
<li><strong>*Parchement Liners:</strong> I highly recommend using parchement liners to ensure easy removal. Otherwise, be sure to brush the muffin tins generously with oil.</li>
<li><strong>A word on adding salt: </strong>I tested this recipe with national cottage cheese brands like Daisy and Good Culture and never needed to add any salt as they were already salty. However, I recommend giving your cottage cheese a taste before deciding whether or not you need to add salt to the egg mixture.</li>
<li><strong>Storage:&nbsp;</strong>Bring leftover egg bites to room temperature and store in an airtight container in the fridge for upto 5 days.</li>
</ul></div></div>
